        {
          "path": "experiments/yolo/SIDEQUEST_SCRIBE_WORKSHOP_MICROTHEORY.md",
          "line": 84,
          "line_end": 88,
          "quote": "Explicitly withdrawn readings include `AROL = WATER`, `OL = WATER`, simultaneous\n`CHOL = HOT` versus `OL = MEDIUM`, `CTHY = DRY`, `D=ASSIGN`, `S=RESUME`,\n`Q=NEXT`, SOL as a confirmed verb, a fixed DESCRIPTION→RECIPE order for the two\nHerbal packets, line equals sentence, a universal diagram-label dictionary,\nand a direct f68↔f69 28-name list. No exact card has a confirmed English meaning.",
          "sha256": "bceabb81a97be7dd6829e7884604cc8db14d7c48241027fcde5bdcd8fc1e1945"
        },
        {
          "path": "experiments/yolo/SIDEQUEST_SCRIBE_WORKSHOP_MICROTHEORY.md",
          "line": 4624,
          "line_end": 4628,
          "quote": "This is better than `AROL = water`. An axis/conduit abstraction can recur in\nplant-root/stalk labels and in tubes, channels and flows; a water noun cannot\nexplain the plant and astronomical counterexamples. On f83r the tempting pair\nis therefore not two translated phrases but two ends/states of one registered\nconduit construction:",
          "sha256": "bceabb81a97be7dd6829e7884604cc8db14d7c48241027fcde5bdcd8fc1e1945"
        }
      ],
